docs: add market badges, README icon, close issue #1 (v1.4.1)

README now opens with the repo icon and three listing badges, each verified
by curl against its live endpoint and linked to the page it describes:
  - dshopen.org (开放插件市场): endpoint badge -> message "已收录 · ♥ 50"
  - dpharness.com: install badge -> "dsh install" + "L4 passed"
  - Awesome REA: "Featured in Awesome REA" (offered in issue #1)

The dsh.so badge is deliberately NOT added: cdn.dsh.so/badge/dsh-rea.svg
resolves, but its page is keyed by plugin name only and currently documents
the fork zhaofeng130/dsh-rea (install command and L1-L5 records are that
repo), so the badge would point readers at someone else repository.

Also verified that dshopen already shows our icon byte-for-byte identical to
icon.svg (716 B), i.e. it reads package.json "icon" - no manifest change was
needed. Issue #1 entry checked item by item and found accurate; replied and
closed as completed.

Runtime is unchanged: cordis.patch.yml, the launcher and scripts are
byte-identical to v1.4.0. Only versions and docs move.
